            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 84-year-old male patient, admitted on 28/04/2019 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests were obtained to exclude secondary pathology. The patient was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout his stay. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. We recommend continuation of his inhaled maintenance therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you have any questions.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
